00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:03.440
Leah: How a person feels about
themselves and many different pressures

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:07.569
growing up can affect a child’s or
young person’s self-esteem, such as

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:12.620
social media, bullying, exams, family
problems, gender issues and abuse.

00:00:15.719 --> 00:00:19.279
Rhiannon: Most children will have dips
in self-esteem as they go through life.

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:24.020
Starting a new school, moving house,
changes in the family and many

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:27.610
other factors can affect a child’s
confidence, but with support from

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:31.529
parents and other adults in their lives
they usually get them through this.

00:00:32.139 --> 00:00:35.450
Leah: Children and young people with
high self-esteem often have a positive

00:00:35.489 --> 00:00:39.459
image of themselves and are confident,
make friends easily, and will try

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:41.140
new things and adapt to change.

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:45.580
They often are happy on their own or in
a group and will try to solve problems

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:50.040
for themselves and if they make mistakes
will learn from them, ultimately

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:51.810
becoming proud of their achievements.

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:56.480
Children and young people with low
self-esteem often have a negative image

00:00:56.480 --> 00:01:02.640
of themselves, they might feel bad, ugly,
unlikeable or stupid, lack in confidence

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:06.240
and are constantly comparing themselves
to their peers in a negative way.

00:01:09.299 --> 00:01:14.220
They may feel lonely and isolated finding
it hard to make and keep friendships

00:01:14.530 --> 00:01:16.600
or feeling victimised by others.

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:21.590
They tend to avoid new things, finding
change hard and can't deal well with

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:26.399
their own failure, putting themselves
down and not proud of achievement, always

00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:27.870
thinking they could have done better.

